-- | Golden differential goldens for the wire conformance corpus (M3 plan
-- D8/D16), the @cabal test@ half of the N11 differential anchor.
--
-- The committed fixtures under @fixtures/@ (the two self-edge fixtures),
-- @fixtures/corpus/@ (generated by @scripts/gen-corpus.hs@), and the fifteen
-- worked-example anchors @examples/<NAME>/example.core.sexp@ (generated by
-- @scripts/gen-worked-examples.hs@) are the single
-- source of truth. Each 'CheckInput' is decoded and run through the real
-- Haskell pipeline ('Lara.Driver.runCheck'); the printed identity-bearing
-- verdict must equal the pinned golden bytes — the exact bytes __both__ drivers
-- emit, cross-checked against the Lean executable semantics by
-- @scripts/differential.sh@ (the real both-drivers differential). These checks
-- let plain @cabal test@ catch regressions without the Lean binary present.
--
-- The fixtures are also guarded to be canonical:
-- @printSExpr (encodeCheckInput input)@ must reproduce the committed bytes, so
-- a hand-edit that is not canonical wire text is rejected.
--
-- The deliberately malformed envelopes under @fixtures/malformed/@ are NOT
-- part of these goldens: they are the negative half of
-- @scripts/differential.sh@ (PR #44 review C8), where both drivers must exit
-- 2 with empty stdout. One anchor, @non-canonical-theory-order.sexp@,
-- additionally pins a per-driver stderr substring there (issue #36
-- re-review): the theory-identity comparison is list-ordered on both
-- drivers, so exit-2-only cannot distinguish the canonical-order rejection
-- from 'TheoryIdentityMismatch' for that envelope.
--
-- Arbitration (plan Global Constraints): the Lean executable is the oracle.
-- These goldens are the agreed bytes; if @differential.sh@ ever shows Lean
-- disagreeing, that is a bug fixed with a recorded note — never a silent
-- re-annotation of a golden here.
--
-- This module reads the fixture files by relative path, so the suite must be
-- run from the package root (as @cabal test@ does).
module DifferentialSpec (differentialSpecProps) where

import Data.List (stripPrefix)

import Test.QuickCheck

